0result.sql
```

Reason:  
Both scripts pull deaths by joining DEATHRECORDS to ENTITYAXISCONDITIONS and filter ICD‑10 descriptions for “vehicle” and “firearm,” so either would return correct counts where data exist.  
However, 0result.sql first builds an explicit list of ages 12‑18 (“ages” CTE) and left‑joins the aggregated results to that list. This guarantees one output row for every required age even when an age would have zero qualifying deaths, fully satisfying the specification “for each age from 12 through 18 (inclusive).”  
The single‑query version (1result.sql) will omit an age entirely if no deaths meet either cause condition, so it is less safe.